<title>UK: First oil tanker since UN deal fixed Iraq-Japan.</title>
<headline>First oil tanker since UN deal fixed Iraq-Japan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first oil tanker to be chartered from Iraq to Japan since the U.N. oil-for-food deal will load from the Iraqi oil terminal of Mina al-Bakr on January 24, shipping brokers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said either the Golden Fountain or the Bourgogne would take 250,000 tonnes of crude for Petrodiamond on behalf of Japan's Mitsubishi at a worldscale rate of W66.</p>
<p>The voyage takes 18 to 20 days. A broker said the fixture was still on subjects, pending U.N. approval of Mitsubishi's 40,000 barrels per day (bpd) sales contract with Iraq.</p>
<p>Two other similar-sized vessels, the Leonidas and the Star Africa, have already been chartered for westwards voyages.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
